ith and some moments even come  directly from experiences she had  growing up in toronto like this slightly  embarrassing one drawing boys and mermen  in my sketchbook secretly under my bed  did anybody else draw exactly like may  does in the movie like if you dug out  some of your old school work with the  margins all doodled on you wouldn't be  able to tell the difference it makes  domi cringe thinking back on the memory  but she's proud of the inclusion in the  film that and the inclusion of four town  simulating her favorite boy bands but it  isn't all about nostalgia for domi it's  also about being the daughter of  immigrants and being the only child of  my overprotective mom and dad  imagine being that one woman in a boy  band billy eilish and phineas o'connell  were stoked to join the turning red team  and write three boy band songs in the  style of nsync it's literally been the  most fun we've had writing lindsay  collins the film's producer said when we  first started talking about billy eilish  and phineas back before they'd won a  billion grammys we could see then how  they had their finger on the pulse we  were big fans when we got approached  about this project we left at the  opportunity honestly who wouldn't leap  at that  true it was very exciting quite  literally changing the face of film and  tv toronto is the most multicultural  city in the world did we mention that  and the team of turning red wanted that  reflected a technology was developed  that would in any frame of a scene  analyze what the representation was on  the screen this was a very helpful tool  because in wide shots they may get the  representation they aim to achieve but  different angles may skew the results  all this kind of diversity that you've  created is it is it actually making it  on the screen in the way that we were  intending not only was the team doing  their best at being culturally diverse  but including details like wheelchair  ramps and insulin patches that's so  awesome that people can see themselves  hey girlfriends what is up  you would never be able to guess that  the actors weren't in the same room or  state it was thanks to domi she knowing  the story she wanted to tell inside out  helping assist the actors to get the  reads she wanted for her movie as the  two lead actors who played mae and her  mom did not record together rosalie and  i both recorded at our separately it at  our own homes  and then they recorded separately at  pixar and los angeles locations later on  the two never actually officially met in  person until the press tour i've been  working on this film for four years and  to finally be here at the world premiere  is surreal sometimes lines get cut and  sometimes great lines get cut we're just  a little bit sad to hear this quirky  canadian relevant pickup line was  replaced are you a beaver cause damn  the line was cut and replaced with a new  even dorkier geometry triangle joke  which like yes it was also great it's  just too bad there wasn't space for both  oh about the hustle am i right  one day there will be a disney  documentary on these guys  while recording for the four town boy  band booth sessions the guys were  goofing around and imitating each other  and it was just a lot of fun for them  insync was the main inspiration for the  music the tracks are written so well  with really tight harmonies that  complement each of their ranges topher  went on to say the songs are absolute  bops there's some fun party tunes um  there's some radio hit and then there's  like also a ballad a really like nice  balance so voice acting sessions that  were actually in a studio are  you  serious  while a lot of the voice acting was  recorded from home there was still  definitely lots of studio time down the  line there's just so many ways to say  something  that like so many different tones of  your voice oh my gosh that's like the  best thing ever we are curious to know  what they had in mind with the gangsters  